*Heading
Simply supported planar beam on two B22 elements: mid-span load, frequency, Euler buckling
** L = 1000, RECT section 20 (out of plane, local 1) x 40 (in plane, local 2), E = 210000,
** nu = 0.3, rho = 7.85e-9 (the beam of planar_pinned_beam.inp).  Abaqus integrates its
** quadratic beams at 2 points along the beam, which makes this mesh exact for the mid-span
** load: P L^3 / (48 E I) + P L / (4 k G A) = 0.9346 (k = 0.85).  Beam theory: f1 = pi /
** (2 L^2) sqrt(E I / (rho A)) = 93.81 Hz, P = pi^2 E I / L^2 = 221079.  ccx 2.23 as B32R (2
** points, as abq2ccx writes it): 0.9985 of the deflection, f1 and P 1.3 % and 1.1 % high; as
** B32 (3 points): 0.76 of the deflection, f1 10.6 % and P 20.8 % high.
